from revise_narratives import revise

revise('searching-for-sita-bibaha',replacements=[
('A musical narration should not automatically be called the film’s original soundtrack. Nor can a poster or a written description reproduce the experience of watching the film. Those limits make the surviving objects more interesting, because they ask us to listen and look closely instead of treating each one as a substitute for everything else.','These musical narrations have not been established as the film’s original soundtrack. Heard alongside a poster or contract, they can still help us explore the world around its making.'),
('The search also changes whose work becomes visible. An artist named in an agreement, a printer on a poster or a musician in a recording may offer another path into the production. Whether a particular document supports that path has to be checked against the document itself.','An artist named in an agreement, a printer on a poster or a musician in a recording may offer another path into the production.'),
('The records inspected for this article establish the project and its approach. They do not confirm a completed film, a release date or a recovered print.','A completed film, release date or recovered print has not been confirmed.')],reason='E13: retain specific soundtrack/project/recoveredprint limits without repetitive process commentary.')
revise('who-keeps-a-film-alive',replacements=[
('The Bhubaneswar workshop brought film and paper conservation, sound, digitisation, cataloguing and archive management into the same programme.[^workshop] That range makes preservation visible as work people can learn. It needs careful hands, technical judgment and the patience to describe an object accurately.','A workshop can begin a working life. Continuing it takes somewhere to practise, experienced colleagues and time paid for the care each object needs.')],reason='E19: avoid repeated skills list; progress from workshop evidence to continuity proposal.')
revise('gourahari-das',replacements=[
('Three recognitions offer different entry points:\n\n- **2012 Sahitya Akademi Award:** *Kanta O’ Anyanya Galpa*, an Odia short-story collection.[^award]\n- **2021 Sahitya Akademi Translation Prize:** *Chheli Chareibara Dina*.[^translation]\n- **2022 Sarala Puraskar:** listed by award organiser IMPaCT.[^sarala]','Alongside the Akademi recognitions attached to his writing and translation, Das received the **2022 Sarala Puraskar**, recorded by award organiser IMPaCT.[^sarala]')],reason='E17: remove repeated awards already tied to works, preserve Sarala and reading routes.')
revise('pratikshya',replacements=[
('The development-stage Film Bazaar entry credits **Roshan Bisoi** as writer and gives April 2021 as a tentative completion date, rather than a release date.[^bazaar] The credit places screenwriting beside the source story in the film’s creative history.','The Film Bazaar entry credits **Roshan Bisoi** as writer, placing screenwriting beside the source story in the film’s creative history.[^bazaar]'),
('It is a trailer, not the complete film; current playback and territorial availability have not been tested here.','Availability may vary by location.')],reason='E18: foreground screenwriter; catalogue developmentdate context stays in source note; simplify trailer-access prose.')
revise('odia-ott',replacements=[
('For a service, paying subscribers help sustain the catalogue. For a filmmaker, the relevant return is the payment agreed for a work and the rights retained for its future. Connecting those two interests is part of building a durable home for Odia stories.\n\nFor viewers, the question is whether a work remains findable and accessible. For makers, it is whether payment and rights arrangements help support the next production. The [cinema overview](/cinema/odia-cinema/#recent-releases-and-the-work-of-reaching-audiences) asks a related question about theatres: how can a willing audience reach the work?','A durable home for these stories must serve both sides of the screen: viewers able to find the work, and makers paid on terms that help them continue. The [economics chapter](cinema-series/cinema-economics.md) follows that question from an audience’s payment towards the next production.'),
('These links open providers or their app listings, not guaranteed access to a particular film. Check current catalogues, territory and payment terms; playback was not tested.','Check the provider’s current catalogue, location and subscription terms.'),
('- **Provider catalogue: [AAO NXT](https://aaonxt.com/).** Homepage checked on 26 October 2026; login and subscription options were visible.','- **Provider catalogue: [AAO NXT](https://aaonxt.com/).**'),
('- **Provider app listing: [Kanccha Lannka on the App Store](https://apps.apple.com/in/app/kanccha-lannka/id1584598214).** Listing checked on 25 October 2026. Descriptions of titles or subtitles do not guarantee access in every location.','- **Provider app listing: [Kanccha Lannka on the App Store](https://apps.apple.com/in/app/kanccha-lannka/id1584598214).**')],reason='E12: combine repeated sustainability closing and remove routine checklog text from reader links.')
